{
  "id": 114881706,
  "iid": 4067,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "802.11 Decryption: Fix AAD Calculation for CCMP when HT-Control present in a QoS Data Frame",
  "description": "The current implementation misses an edge case, where bit 15 of the FC Field must be zeroed in case a QoS Control field is present (IEEE 802.11 12.5.3.3.3) during the preparation of the AAD, which results in a wrong AAD and subsequently in the failure of the packet decryption for QoS Data Frame carrying a HT Control Field (indicated by bit 15 set to 1).\nIn addition the field 14 must always be 1, which is ensured explicitly (the author is not sure if the code is reachable by frames which do not have bit 14 set to one).",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2021-09-01T11:20:38.096Z",
  "updated_at": "2021-09-07T15:45:21.990Z",
