  "commits_data": [
    {
      "id": "e5e37add9af3bdf0d69662ceb2e5bad420528c02",
      "short_id": "e5e37add",
      "created_at": "2021-09-02T10:56:02.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "cfc60b3f6ef9a20d46818be203f344171e7a1912"
      ],
      "title": "802.11 Decrypt: Fix AAD Calculation when HT-Control present in a QoS Data Frame",
      "message": "802.11 Decrypt: Fix AAD Calculation when HT-Control present in a QoS Data Frame\n\nThe current implementation misses an edge case, where bit 15 of the FC Field\nmust be zeroed in case a QoS Control field is present (IEEE 802.11 12.5.3.3.3),\nwhich results in a wrong AAD and subsequently in the failure of the packet\ndecryption for QoS Data Frame carrying a HT Control Field (indicated by bit\n15 set to 1).\n\nIn addition the field 14 must be 1, which is ensured explicitly (the author is\nnot sure if the code is reachable by frames which do not have bit 14 set to\none).\n",
      "author_name": "Marius Preuten",
      "author_email": "marius.preuten@lancom.de",
      "authored_date": "2021-09-01T12:54:18.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2021-09-02T10:56:02.000+00:00",
